Are you a DevOps engineer, developer, or architect trying to keep your codebase clean, secure, and maintainable?

Let’s simplify how SonarQube works and how it helps improve software quality! 🛠️✨

🔍 𝐖𝐡𝐚𝐭 𝐢𝐬 𝐒𝐨𝐧𝐚𝐫𝐐𝐮𝐛𝐞?
SonarQube is a code health scanner 🩺 used in CI/CD pipelines to automatically check:
✅ Bugs 🐞
✅ Vulnerabilities 🔐
✅ Code Smells 👃
✅ Duplications 🔁
✅ Test Coverage 📊

🚦 𝐖𝐡𝐚𝐭’𝐬 𝐚 𝐐𝐮𝐚𝐥𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐆𝐚𝐭𝐞?
Think of it like a traffic signal for your pipeline:
 If your code fails certain criteria (like low test coverage or critical bugs), the build fails ❌

𝐓𝐲𝐩𝐢𝐜𝐚𝐥 𝐫𝐮𝐥𝐞𝐬 𝐢𝐧𝐜𝐥𝐮𝐝𝐞:
Code Coverage > 80%
No critical bugs or new code smells
Duplications < 3%
📊 Code Coverage = Test Confidence

It tells how much of your code is tested by unit tests.
 More coverage → fewer surprises in production ✅
🔐 Security Hotspots

Spots in code that may need attention:
Hardcoded secrets 🔑
Unsafe inputs 🚨

📏 Code Smells & Duplications
Code smells = Maintainability issues 👃
 Duplications = Copy-paste nightmares 🔁
 Both hurt long-term code health!

⚙️ 𝐓𝐲𝐩𝐢𝐜𝐚𝐥 𝐃𝐞𝐯𝐎𝐩𝐬 𝐖𝐨𝐫𝐤𝐟𝐥𝐨𝐰
